# Temperance marker — 1.9.21 release + cli#479
- date: 2026-11-07
- branch: release-1.9.21
- scope-decision: Right thing — ship the install-output collapse (#477, merged
  as ec1b875) to npm. Right way — `npm run bump patch`, which touches all four
  version files together. Hand-editing package.json leaves three stale, per
  memory feedback_use_npm_run_bump_not_hand_edit.
- bundled, and why: the bump refused with "npm run build failed" while the
  build had just succeeded. Root cause is a defect in the bump script itself
  (cli#479). The release cannot be verified without that fix, so the two ride
  together per .claude/rules/pr-strategy.md "tight coupling that breaks atomic
  verification". Not an operator preference.
- what it can break: the bump script runs on every release. The fix is one
  expression on a line that always threw, so the change can only reduce
  failures. Default-runner behavior now has a test; it had none.
- drift-trigger: if this starts touching publish.yml or the gate script, stop.
  Neither is in scope.
